FIX CAR-SELECT CRASH (815): scattered-locals wild write in FUN_0044e600 (stat bars)

FUN_0044e600 @0x44e600 rebuilds the three car-select stat-bar sprite-pointer arrays
(Acceleration / Top Speed / Grip, 5 bar-segment sprites each) whenever race_car changes
(Toggle_Car in Select_Car's cycle path). Each array is a 5-POINTER contiguous stack block
-- asm offsets -0x24..-0x10 (accel), -0x38..-0x24 (top speed), -0x4c..-0x38 (grip) -- but
Ghidra split the 5th element of each into a SEPARATE local (puStack_14 / puStack_28 /
puStack_3c) beside a `[4]` array. The body then walks each block CONTIGUOUSLY:
`**(short **)((int)local_24 + iVar4)` with iVar4 = 0,4,8,12,16 (the `iVar2 < 0x14` loops
touch all 5 slots). At iVar4=16 that dereferences element [4] -- which in C is NOT the
split-off puStack_XX (gcc places it wherever it likes, not necessarily adjacent), so it
reads a garbage stack pointer and writes 0xfa/0x7c/0xfc18 THROUGH it -> wild write ->
browser tab crash / native heap corruption the instant you cycle cars in Car Select.
This is the reported car-select crash.

Faithful fix: coalesce each split [4]+puStack pair into the true 5-element array the asm
uses (local_24[5]/local_38[5]/local_4c[5]); the 5th assignment goes to local_XX[4]. An
array is always contiguous, so `(int)local_24 + iVar4` now spans exactly the intended 5
slots and never touches an unrelated variable. No access crosses a 5-block boundary, so
three separate [5] arrays reproduce the original 15-pointer stack region exactly.
Scattered-locals class (edge-sorter vertex arrays, Setup_Sprite info blocks, TextureDentHi
dent-uv blocks patch 655).

